From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prplOS buildsystem <noreply@prplos>
Date: Mon, 28 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audisp: fix NULL plugin_dir segfault when config file is missing

When /etc/audisp/audispd.conf does not exist, load_config() returns 0
early without calling sanity_check(). sanity_check() is the only code
path that initialises plugin_dir to its default value
("/etc/audisp/plugins.d/"). As a result plugin_dir remains NULL and the
subsequent opendir(daemon_config.plugin_dir) call in load_plugin_conf()
triggers a SIGSEGV (si_code=SEGV_MAPERR, si_addr=NULL).

Fix by calling sanity_check() in the ENOENT branch instead of returning
0 directly, so that plugin_dir (and any other defaulted fields) are
always initialised regardless of whether the configuration file exists.

Signed-off-by: prplOS buildsystem <noreply@prplos>
---
 audisp/audispd-config.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/audisp/audispd-config.c
+++ b/audisp/audispd-config.c
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@ int load_config(daemon_conf_t *config, c
 		}
 		audit_msg(LOG_WARNING,
 			"Config file %s doesn't exist, skipping", file);
-		return 0;
+		return sanity_check(config, file);
 	}
 	fd = rc;

